# AttaLambda @VERSION@

This is an unpublished development artifact for internal testing on Linux
x86-64. It is not a public release.

The archive contains the `attalambda` executable, its private Racket runtime, and four
example `.attl` programs. A separate Racket installation is neither required nor
used.

From the extracted `@ROOT_NAME@` directory:

```text
./bin/attalambda --help
./bin/attalambda --version
./bin/attalambda examples/hello.attl
```

Every source file must use the lowercase `.attl` extension and begin with this
exact declaration:

```text
#lang attalambda
```

`attalambda FILE.attl` executes with the launching process's filesystem and network
authority. This development artifact does not sandbox programs, ask for
permissions, or make backups.

Verify the archive against the sibling `SHA256SUMS` file before extracting it.
The internal `BUILD-MANIFEST.txt` identifies the source revision, toolchain,
payload inventory, and observed Linux system-library assumptions.
